Third-party data and attribution
--------------------------------

OpenStreetMap. rail_data/processed/osm_stations.csv is derived from an
OpenStreetMap extract (Overpass API). (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available
under the Open Database Licence (ODbL) 1.0: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
That table is a derived database; if you redistribute it, keep this attribution
and share it under the ODbL. The Apache-2.0 licence of this repository does not
apply to it. The raw extract is not redistributed.

DataMeet railways collection. fetch_rail_data.py can download DataMeet's station,
train and schedule JSON files (labelled CC0 by DataMeet, https://github.com/datameet/railways).
No DataMeet data is used to build the processed tables and none is redistributed
here, so no attribution is required; it is credited because the script fetches it.

Indian Railways documents. Working time tables, station working rules and
diagrams, and the High Density Network report are published by Indian Railways
zones and the Railway Board. They are not redistributed here. The processed
tables hold facts extracted from them (running times, loop lengths, train
timings). See SOURCES.md for every document and its URL. The publishers' own
terms apply to the original documents.
